
Sqlkit has been written by sandro dentella <sandro@e-den.it>


In the late '90 I developed as my first jon in GUI tksql a similar library in
tcl/tk that I still need to use. 

Sqlkit is meant as a replacement, better under all possible points of view:
better language, nicer grafical toolkit, based on a serious ORM.


The first version of SqlTable was started by Michele Comitini 
The module optionparse was written by Michele Simionato 
The module dateedit was written by Fabian Sturm
the multiline renderer was set to pygtk list by Osmo Salomaa

